    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math education by adapting explanations to individual learning styles, offering instant feedback, and demystifying abstract concepts through relatable analogies. They can identify knowledge gaps, suggest targeted practice, and make math less intimidating. For students like me — unemployed, with low conscientiousness but high openness — AI could reignite curiosity without pressure. In classrooms, they serve as tutors, not replacements, enhancing engagement without replacing deep understanding."
